  "code_explanation": [
    {
      "text": "The first-year routine starts I at zero, sums INVS across sectors, then floors I at 0.001 and sets IGCF to I. Equality to the sector sum is conditional on that floor being inactive; it is not an unconditional identity.",
      "code_evidence": [
        "initial_sum",
        "initial_floor",
        "initial_order"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SISPL is initialized from INVS/IGCF. Forecast INVS is IGCF times these origin shares. The active forecast inventory calculation sets I to IGCF plus the summed supply-minus-final-demand residual; it does not add that residual back into INVS. Forecast equality is not required, but can occur when the relevant terms cancel.",
      "code_evidence": [
        "origin_shares",
        "origin_allocation",
        "inventory"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The dispatcher calls the SAM allocation before the economic routine that calls the inventory calculation. Exogenous I replacement follows its assignment, and a dyadic-trade path can repeat the calculation. These conditions and saved-output timing must be checked before claiming the equation explains a particular saved run.",
      "code_evidence": [
        "forecast_order",
        "nested_call",
        "inventory",
        "dyadic_recalculation"
      ]
    }
  ],
